      "content": "That \"historical protective coating\" angle is a good starting point, but I'm worried the technical committee is going to look right through it. The scans aren't just showing a surface layer; they're showing the polymer signature deep within the foundational pigment strata, not just on the varnish.\n\nIf I tell the Board it's just a \"documented conservation treatment,\" they're going to ask why a treatment from the 17th or 18th century would show up as a modern, integrated synthetic binder in the base layers. How do we explain that level of penetration without it looking like we're trying to mask a forgery?",
